{{!
    @template message_output_popup/shopping_cart_popover

    This template will render the shopping_cart popover for the navigation bar.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * All data attributes are required

    Context variables required for this template:
    * userid the logged in user id
    * urls The URLs for the popover

    Example context (json):
    {
        "itemid": 3,
        "componentname": "mod_booking",
        "area": "main",
        "price": 133,
        "expirationtime": 1642155164,
        "itemname": "Tenniscourse"
    }

}}
{{!
    A real <button>, not a <div>: this price chip adds the slot to the cart when it is clicked, but
    it had neither a tabindex nor a role, so it was unreachable by keyboard and announced as plain
    table text. Its visible content is only the price, which says nothing about what activating it
    does - hence the aria-label naming the slot.

    "free" is a boolean, and mustache renders false as an empty string. Writing the value out
    explicitly keeps data-bookable="1" for the bookable case (the timeslot table styles that value)
    and produces a real "false" for the other one, which the not-bookable styling expects.
}}
<button type="button" class="mt-0 mb-0 ps-1 pe-1 pt-0 pb-0 wb_shopping_cart booking-button-area"
        id="btn-{{componentname}}-{{area}}-{{itemid}}"
        {{#slot}}
            aria-label="{{#str}} addtocartitem, local_shopping_cart, {{slot}} {{/str}}"
        {{/slot}}
        {{^free}}aria-disabled="true"{{/free}}
        data-itemname="{{slot}}"
        data-itemid="{{itemid}}"
        {{#nojs}}
            data-nojs="1"
        {{/nojs}}
        data-userid="{{userid}}"
        data-objecttable="local_shopping_cart"
        data-component="{{componentname}}"
        data-area="{{area}}"
        data-bookable="{{#free}}1{{/free}}{{^free}}false{{/free}}">
        {{price}} {{currency}} {{tag}}
</button>

{{#js}}
    require(['local_shopping_cart/cart'], function(fn) {
        fn.buttoninit("{{itemid}}", "{{componentname}}", "{{area}}");
    });
{{/js}}
